{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://github.com/agourakis82/darwin-atlas/schemas/window_operator_profile.schema.json",
  "title": "DOSA window operator profile (mini-pipeline JSONL line)",
  "description": "One line of the deterministic JSONL emitted by the Sounio mini-pipeline (sounio/src/fasta_stream_fixture.sio --pipeline). Serialization constraints that JSON Schema cannot express are normative text: object members MUST appear in the order listed in 'required', numbers delta_R/delta_RC and the k-mer imbalance ratios MUST serialize with exactly six fractional digits, integers without padding, strings are restricted to [A-Za-z0-9._-] so no JSON escaping ever occurs, and each line is terminated by a single LF. Excluded windows (status=excluded) MUST carry null for every POSITIONAL metric field and effective_count 0; the positional status never forces k-mer fields to null. K-mer fields use the masked policy: for each k in 1..8 the triple (kmer_<k>_effective_count, kmer_<k>_unavailable_reason, six reverse/rc imbalance fields) is either fully null (k above the configured k_max), reason INSUFFICIENT_EFFECTIVE_KMERS with an integer count and six nulls (count below kmer_min_effective_count), or reason null with integer numerator/denominator fields where denominator == kmer_<k>_effective_count. When status=ok, effective_count and denominator equal window_length. Schema 0.2.0 supersedes 0.1.0 by adding parameters_sha256, the unavailable-reason fields, and k=5..8; 0.1.0 field interpretations are unchanged.",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "metric_version",
    "parameters_sha256",
    "assembly_accession_version",
    "sequence_accession_version",
    "replicon_class",
